  "body": "Found while building a probe test kit for PR #583 (Tormach probing, #575), 2026-11-09.\n\n**Today:**\n- **Setup:** an inch document with a 3 × 2 × 1 in box stock equal to the part (Z -1..0), and one Probe operation (Z top-face touch). There are no cutting ops.\n- **What happens:** posting succeeds but reports a non-blocking note: \"stock sim did not judge this program: invalid stock simulation setup: stock box and cell must be finite, box non-empty, cell positive\".\n- **Why it's wrong:** the stock is finite and non-empty, so the message names the wrong cause. A probe-only program removes no stock, so the program stock sim has nothing to judge, but it should say that (or say nothing), not report an invalid setup.\n\n**Expected:** a program with no material-removing moves either skips the stock sim with an accurate note (e.g. \"no cutting moves - nothing to simulate\") or runs it trivially clean. A genuinely invalid stock setup keeps its by-name refusal.\n\n**Done means:**\n- a test posts a probe-only program and gets no misleading \"invalid stock simulation setup\" note;\n- a test with a degenerate stock still gets the real refusal.\n\nRelated: #575 / PR #583, #521.",
